---
// MCP tools reference, rendered from the server's own tools/list answer
// (src/data/mcp-tools.json, regenerated by scripts/update-mcp-tools.mjs).
import Docs from '../../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Callout from '../../../components/Callout.astro';
import { groups, tools, meta } from './_mcp-tools';

const title = 'MCP tools';
const description = `The ${tools.length} tools barrel_server registers on its MCP endpoint, with their arguments, generated from the server's tools/list answer.`;
const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'call-a-tool', text: 'Call a tool' },
  ...groups.map((g) => ({ depth: 2, slug: g.slug, text: g.title })),
];
const server = meta.barrelServer ? `barrel_server ${meta.barrelServer}` : 'barrel_server';

const callExample = `curl -X POST localhost:8080/mcp \\
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -H 'accept: application/json, text/event-stream' \\
  -H "mcp-session-id: $SID" \\
  -H 'mcp-protocol-version: ${meta.protocolVersion}' \\
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"tools/call",
       "params":{"name":"doc_get",
       "arguments":{"db":"notes","id":"note-1"}}}'`;
---

<Docs title={title} description={description} slug="reference/mcp-tools" headings={headings}>
  <p>
    This is every tool barrel_server registers on its <code>/mcp</code> endpoint, with the arguments each one takes.
    Use it when you write a client or a prompt that calls Barrel tools and need the exact names and argument shapes.
    The page is generated from the <code>tools/list</code> answer of {server} (MCP protocol {meta.protocolVersion},
    engine {meta.serverInfo.name} {meta.serverInfo.version}), captured on {meta.generated}, so it matches what a client sees.
  </p>
  <p>
    The same list is published as JSON at <a href="/docs/reference/mcp-tools.json"><code>/docs/reference/mcp-tools.json</code></a>.
    To set up the endpoint, see the <a href="/docs/guides/mcp">MCP guide</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="call-a-tool">Call a tool</h2>
  <p>
    Send <code>initialize</code> first and keep the <code>mcp-session-id</code> header it returns,
    then <code>notifications/initialized</code>. A <code>tools/call</code> answers as server-sent events
    (<code>data:</code> frames); the result is JSON text content.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock code={callExample} lang="shell" label="Shell" />
  <ul>
    <li>On a server with <code>auth</code> configured, add <code>Authorization: Bearer</code> with a server token or a <code>bsp_</code> capability token. The endpoint accepts bearer tokens only, not signed requests or mTLS.</li>
    <li>A capability token can call a tool only within its space and rights; a denied call returns a result with <code>isError: true</code>, such as <code>{'{"error":"forbidden","db":"notes"}'}</code>.</li>
    <li>Annotations are hints from the server: <em>read only</em> tools change nothing, <em>destructive</em> tools delete or replace, <em>idempotent</em> tools can be repeated safely.</li>
  </ul>

  {groups.map((g) => (
    <section>
      <h2 id={g.slug}>{g.title}</h2>
      {g.tools.map((t) => (
        <div class="mt">
          <h3 id={t.name}><code>{t.name}</code></h3>
          {t.marks.length > 0 && (
            <p class="mt-marks">{t.marks.map((m) => <span class="mt-mark">{m}</span>)}</p>
          )}
          <p>{t.description}</p>
          {t.args.length === 0
            ? <p class="muted small">No arguments.</p>
            : (
              <table>
                <thead><tr><th scope="col">Argument</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Required</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                  {t.args.map((a) => (
                    <tr>
                      <td><code>{a.name}</code></td>
                      <td>{a.type}</td>
                      <td>{a.required ? 'yes' : 'no'}</td>
                      <td>{a.description}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            )}
        </div>
      ))}
    </section>
  ))}

  <Callout label="Note">
    <p>The schema marks only <code>query</code> as required for <code>context_query</code>; the server also needs one of <code>contexts</code> or <code>working_set</code>. The <code>db_info</code> description mentions a document count, but the info it returns has none.</p>
  </Callout>
</Docs>

<style>
  .mt { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 4px; }
  .mt h3 { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .mt-marks { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .mt-mark { font-size: var(--step--1); font-weight: 600; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 6px; background: var(--paper-2); }
  td:first-child code { white-space: nowrap; }
</style>
